<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 21 July, from 356 BCE to 1969.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">356 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,670 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander the Great is born in Pella</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alexander, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a>, was born by the traditional dating around 20 or 21 July. By his death at 32 he had conquered an empire stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1588 CE <span class="tih-ago">438 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English ships first engage the Spanish Armada off Plymouth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The English fleet under Lord Howard and Drake attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Armada</a> off Plymouth (21 July Old Style). The running fight up the Channel ended at Gravelines and in the Armada's disastrous voyage home.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1773 CE <span class="tih-ago">253 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Clement XIV suppresses the Jesuits</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under pressure from the Catholic monarchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal, Clement XIV dissolved the Society of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>. The order survived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and was restored worldwide in 1814.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1798 CE <span class="tih-ago">228 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon defeats the Mamluks at the Battle of the Pyramids</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French infantry squares broke the charges of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> cavalry near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. The victory gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where his expedition's scholars laid the foundations of modern Egyptology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1925 CE <span class="tih-ago">101 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Scopes is found guilty of teaching evolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Dayton jury convicted teacher John Scopes of breaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>'s ban on teaching human evolution, and he was fined 100 dollars. The verdict was later overturned on a technicality.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1969 CE <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Armstrong and Aldrin lift off from the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After about 21 hours on the lunar surface, Armstrong and Aldrin fired the ascent stage of Eagle to rejoin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-collins">Michael Collins</a> in lunar orbit. They left a plaque reading 'We came in peace for all mankind'.</p></div></li></ol>
